Z||000001||ig88vsbobafett||12-29-2001||06:57 PM||||Not that i know of unless you have smart cops||||reg||1
Z||000002||Master_Sushi||12-29-2001||08:44 PM||||My cat somehow disappeared from my fiero. I have an 84SE 4 speed. With it gone I seem to have a little more high RPM power. Which is what the duke could use more of. The exhaust sounds a little more "riceish" though. I think it was worth it. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Smoooooth GT||12-29-2001||08:54 PM||||As far as I know...  You do gain a lil' HP BUT.. you loose some torque... <BR>Someone stole mine..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I really did'nt feel a difference....<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">                           <BR><A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A>   <BR>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<P>"Smoooooth GT"<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, side scoop's, sail scoop's, ZR-1 hood scoop, decklid scoop, BMW Z~3 vent's, 308 headlight cover's, Custom front and rear fascia's...smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||SLYGUY||12-29-2001||09:02 PM||||Here in So. Cal. we don't have that option. We have to have it along with the EGR for the smog test.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I don't run my GT hard, so having the torque at low rpm is a good thing.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000005||88CoupeV6||12-30-2001||09:26 AM||||I had no cat on my 88GT and I put one on I got from <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rodneydickman.com</A>  to pass the smog test. I was going to take it off after the test but, I actually feel more power and the car is throatier sounding with the cat. I also noticed a 2-4 mpg increase. I am keeping my high flow cats on.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||7
